{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"a8f1a005-6197-4ac8-b6c3-3f7619cec3c7","agentId":"a486d3f9206a2b09a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Audit Phase 3C 路线图 P1 #13：Compiler optimization (`-march=native`, LTO, PGO)，claim \"+6-12% from march+LTO; +5-10% PGO\"。\n\n## 项目背景\n\n终末地工业规划器 70×70 网格 266 设施 exact LBBD 求解器。OR-Tools 9.15.6755 通过官方 manylinux wheel 安装到 CachyOS Linux。硬件 i9-13900KS（Raptor Lake，AVX2 / AVX-VNNI / 部分 AVX-512 disabled by Intel decree on consumer parts）。Python 3.13 / 3.14。\n\n## 原始 claim\n\n- 路线图 (`/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd/docs/phase3c_optimization_roadmap_v1.md`) 第 67 行：\n  > | 13 | **Compiler optimization (-march, LTO, PGO)** | R6 `aa2cd8e2e60b20719` | +6-12% from march+LTO; +5-10% PGO | 1 day + 2-3 days | ~5-10× |\n- 来源 transcript: `/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd/docs/research/agent_transcripts/aa2cd8e2e60b20719.output`\n\n## Audit 任务（按顺序）\n\n1. **Read R6 transcript** (`aa2cd8e2e60b20719.output`) 找 #13 段：数字 \"+6-12%\" / \"+5-10% PGO\" 怎么来的（OR-Tools 官方 benchmark? Generic SAT solver paper? Agent 估?）。\n\n2. **OR-Tools manylinux wheel 默认编译 flags**：\n   - manylinux 标准要求 `-march=x86-64-v2` 或更保守（保 portability），所以 wheel 几乎肯定不带 `-march=native`\n   - 但 LTO / PGO 在 OR-Tools 自己 build script 里有没有？查 GitHub `google/or-tools` 仓库（WebSearch 或 WebFetch）：`Makefile`, `BUILD.bazel`, `ortools/cpp_build.bzl`, `cmake/cpp.cmake` 看默认 flags\n   - 验证：manylinux wheel 是不是 `-O2 / -O3 -fno-plt` 这种基线，还是已经带 LTO\n\n3. **-march=native 在 i9-13900KS 上的实际增益**：\n   - i9-13900KS 支持 AVX2、AVX-VNNI、F16C、BMI2、ADX 等。AVX-512 在 consumer Raptor Lake 上 disabled。\n   - CP-SAT 哪些代码路径会用 AVX/SIMD？（hint：CP-SAT 主体是 CDCL SAT solver 跟 LP relaxation glue 到 GLOP，热点是 propagation、conflict analysis、LP simplex）\n   - SAT solver 通常 SIMD 收益 < 5%（control flow heavy），LP simplex 倒可能 +5-10%（vector dot product）。我们工作负载 master+binding+routing 各自 SIMD-amenability 估一下。\n\n4. **LTO 真实增益**：\n   - 如果 OR-Tools 默认已开 LTO（wheel 看 `nm -D` 或 strings 也许能看到），rebuild 加 LTO = 0% gain\n   - 如果默认没开，典型 LTO 在大型 C++ 项目 +3-8%\n   - 用 WebFetch 查 OR-Tools 官方 build doc 或最近 issue/PR 找证据\n\n5. **PGO 真实情况**：\n   - OR-Tools 有没有官方 PGO build option（不只是 -fprofile-generate / -fprofile-use 通用选项）？典型 PGO 在 SAT/MIP solver 上 +5-15% 是 textbook 数字（参考 PGO 在 Clang / GCC 自身的 +5-10%）\n   - workflow 真实成本：rebuild + 跑代表 workload + rebuild = \"2-3 days\" 是不是低估了 OR-Tools build 30-60 min × 2 + workload coverage 设计时间\n   - 我们项目 168h workload 怎么提取代表样本来 PGO 训练（要避免 overfit 到训练 candidate）\n\n6. **修正后的真实 stack gain**：\n   - march=native: ~? %\n   - LTO 增量（如果 wheel 没开）: ~? %\n   - PGO 增量: ~? %\n   - 总 stack vs claim \"+11-22%（6-12 + 5-10 加和）\"\n\n## 输出格式（不超过 700 字，中文 OK）\n\n```\n## 1. claim 出处\n[transcript 里 #13 段 + 数字源头判断]\n\n## 2. OR-Tools wheel 默认编译 flags\n[查到的事实 + URL]\n\n## 3. -march=native 真实增益估\n[i9-13900KS 指令集 + CP-SAT SIMD-amenability]\n\n## 4. LTO 真实增益估\n[wheel 默认是否已开 + 增量]\n\n## 5. PGO 真实情况\n[OR-Tools 是否官方支持 + 工作量估真实]\n\n## verdict\nGO / GO-WITH-CAVEATS / PARTIALLY_REFUTED / REFUTED\n修正 stack gain X-Y%（vs claim 11-22%）\n3-4 行理由\n```\n\n## 操作准则\n\n- 必须 read transcript 文件\n- 必须用 WebFetch / WebSearch 查 OR-Tools 官方 GitHub 仓库（具体 commit / file URL）\n- 不要凭训练数据估\n- 保持简洁\n\n开始。"},"uuid":"358442bd-a6bf-4b2f-a66f-b526927c9c73","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:02:46.899Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"358442bd-a6bf-4b2f-a66f-b526927c9c73","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a486d3f9206a2b09a","attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_delta","addedNames":["CronCreate","CronDelete","CronList","EnterWorktree","ExitWorktree","Monitor","NotebookEdit","PushNotification","RemoteTrigger","TaskCreate","TaskGet","TaskList","TaskStop","TaskUpdate","WebFetch","WebSearch"],"addedLines":["CronCreate","CronDelete","CronList","EnterWorktree","ExitWorktree","Monitor","NotebookEdit","PushNotification","RemoteTrigger","TaskCreate","TaskGet","TaskList","TaskStop","TaskUpdate","WebFetch","WebSearch"],"removedNames":[],"readdedNames":[]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"02d41845-a940-4e2a-bbbc-3e296393edef","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:02:46.904Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"02d41845-a940-4e2a-bbbc-3e296393edef","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a486d3f9206a2b09a","attachment":{"type":"skill_listing","content":"- update-config: Use this skill to configure the Claude Code harness via settings.json. Automated behaviors (\"from now on when X\", \"each time X\", \"whenever X\", \"before/after X\") require hooks configured in settings.json - the harness executes these, not Claude, so memory/preferences cannot fulfill them. Also use for: permissions (\"allow X\", \"add permission\", \"move permission to\"), env vars (\"set X=Y\"), hook troubleshooting, or any changes to settings.json/settings.local.json files. Examples: \"allow npm commands\", \"add bq permission to global settings\", \"move permission to user settings\", \"set DEBUG=true\", \"when claude stops show X\". For simple settings like theme/model, suggest the /config command.\n- keybindings-help: Use when the user wants to customize keyboard shortcuts, rebind keys, add chord bindings, or modify ~/.claude/keybindings.json. Examples: \"rebind ctrl+s\", \"add a chord shortcut\", \"change the submit key\", \"customize keybindings\".\n- simplify: Review changed code for reuse, quality, and efficiency, then fix any issues found.\n- fewer-permission-prompts: Scan your transcripts for common read-only Bash and MCP tool calls, then add a prioritized allowlist to project .claude/settings.json to reduce permission prompts.\n- loop: Run a prompt or slash command on a recurring interval (e.g. /loop 5m /foo). Omit the interval to let the model self-pace. - When the user wants to set up a recurring task, poll for status, or run something repeatedly on an interval (e.g. \"check the deploy every 5 minutes\", \"keep running /babysit-prs\"). Do NOT invoke for one-off tasks.\n- schedule: Create, update, list, or run scheduled remote agents (routines) that execute on a cron schedule. - When the user wants to schedule a recurring remote agent, set up automated tasks, create a cron job for Claude Code, or manage their scheduled agents/routines. Also use when the user wants a one-time scheduled run (\"run this once at 3pm\", \"remind me to check X tomorrow\").\n- claude-api: Build, debug, and optimize Claude API / Anthropic SDK apps. Apps built with this skill should include prompt caching. Also handles migrating existing Claude API code between Claude model versions (4.5 → 4.6, 4.6 → 4.7, retired-model replacements).\nTRIGGER when: code imports `anthropic`/`@anthropic-ai/sdk`; user asks for the Claude API, Anthropic SDK, or Managed Agents; user adds/modifies/tunes a Claude feature (caching, thinking, compaction, tool use, batch, files, citations, memory) or model (Opus/Sonnet/Haiku) in a file; questions about prompt caching / cache hit rate in an Anthropic SDK project.\nSKIP: file imports `openai`/other-provider SDK, filename like `*-openai.py`/`*-generic.py`, provider-neutral code, general programming/ML.\n- init: Initialize a new CLAUDE.md file with codebase documentation\n- review: Review a pull request\n- security-review: Complete a security review of the pending changes on the current branch","skillCount":10,"isInitial":true},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6448c523-391e-4661-9a37-1286ce93d7dd","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:02:46.904Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
