{"parentUuid":"0455b956-65c2-4174-b15e-93a7c2cfdfa4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"a8f1a005-6197-4ac8-b6c3-3f7619cec3c7","agentId":"a486d3f9206a2b09a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013vjYszzhUNSpThuy52shyR","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"or-tools manylinux wheel build flags PGO LTO 2025 OR-Tools 9.x release optimization\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - pypa/manylinux: Python wheels that work on any linux (almost) · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/pypa/manylinux\"},{\"title\":\"Building manylinux Python wheels | Opensource.com\",\"url\":\"https://opensource.com/article/19/2/manylinux-python-wheels\"},{\"title\":\"Distribution - Maturin User Guide\",\"url\":\"https://www.maturin.rs/distribution.html\"},{\"title\":\"PEP 513 – A Platform Tag for Portable Linux Built Distributions | peps.python.org\",\"url\":\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0513/\"},{\"title\":\"[pacman-dev] LTO and PGO build options\",\"url\":\"https://pacman-dev.archlinux.narkive.com/lE0g1cTt/lto-and-pgo-build-options\"},{\"title\":\"Python builds — Unofficial Python Development (Victor's notes) documentation\",\"url\":\"https://pythondev.readthedocs.io/builds.html\"},{\"title\":\"manylinux rust/pyo3 build guide | mike bommarito\",\"url\":\"https://michaelbommarito.com/wiki/programming/tools/manylinux-rust-builds/\"},{\"title\":\"LTO and PGO Possibilities\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/NatLabRockies/EnergyPlus/wiki/LTO-and-PGO-Possibilities\"},{\"title\":\"awesome-pgo/article/article.md at main · zamazan4ik/awesome-pgo\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/zamazan4ik/awesome-pgo/blob/main/article/article.md\"},{\"title\":\"PEP 600 – Future 'manylinux' Platform Tags for Portable Linux ...\",\"url\":\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0600/\"}]\n\nThe search results provide general information about manylinux wheel building, PGO, and LTO, but don't contain specific details about OR-Tools 9.x build flags. Let me search more specifically for OR-Tools releases and optimization flags.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Release Notes | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/support/release_notes\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/releases\"},{\"title\":\"v9.12 · google/or-tools · Discussion #4544\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/4544\"},{\"title\":\"ortools Changelog\",\"url\":\"https://data.safetycli.com/packages/pypi/ortools/changelog\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools - Google Optimization Tools - Browse /v9.12 at SourceForge.net\",\"url\":\"https://sourceforge.net/projects/or-tools.mirror/files/v9.12/\"},{\"title\":\"ortools · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/ortools/\"},{\"title\":\"NuGet Gallery | Google.OrTools 9.15.6755\",\"url\":\"https://www.nuget.org/packages/Google.OrTools/\"},{\"title\":\"NuGet Gallery | Google.OrTools.runtime.osx-x64 9.12.4544\",\"url\":\"https://www.nuget.org/packages/Google.OrTools.runtime.osx-x64/9.12.4544\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools-discuss - Google Groups\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss\"},{\"title\":\"Toolkk\",\"url\":\"https://www.toolkk.com/en/posts/tools-summary-2025-12\"}]\n\nNow let me search more specifically for OR-Tools build configuration and CMake optimization flags.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Testing 3 Approaches for Optimizing the Performance of C++ Apps: LTO, PGO, and Unity Builds | The CLion Blog\",\"url\":\"https://blog.jetbrains.com/clion/2022/05/testing-3-approaches-performance-cpp_apps/\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Build Configurations — LLVM 23.0.0git documentation\",\"url\":\"https://llvm.org/docs/AdvancedBuilds.html\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Build Configurations — LLVM 20.0.0git documentation\",\"url\":\"https://rocm.docs.amd.com/projects/llvm-project/en/latest/LLVM/llvm/html/AdvancedBuilds.html\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Build Configurations — LLVM 18.1.0rc documentation\",\"url\":\"https://releases.llvm.org/18.1.0/docs/AdvancedBuilds.html\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Build Configurations — LLVM 18.0.0git documentation\",\"url\":\"https://rocm.docs.amd.com/projects/llvm-project/en/docs-6.3.3/LLVM/llvm/html/AdvancedBuilds.html\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Build Configurations — LLVM 16.0.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://prereleases.llvm.org/16.0.0/rc3/docs/AdvancedBuilds.html\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Build Configurations — LLVM 18.1.1 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://releases.llvm.org/18.1.1/docs/AdvancedBuilds.html\"},{\"title\":\"How To Build Clang and LLVM with Profile-Guided Optimizations — LLVM 23.0.0git documentation\",\"url\":\"https://llvm.org/docs/HowToBuildWithPGO.html\"},{\"title\":\"cc Compiler Options: The Complete Guide to Flags, Optimization, Debugging, and Linking\",\"url\":\"https://www.cleverence.com/articles/oracle-documentation/cc-compiler-options-5938/\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Build Configurations — LLVM 19.0.0git documentation\",\"url\":\"https://rocmdocs.amd.com/projects/llvm-project/en/latest/LLVM/llvm/html/AdvancedBuilds.html\"}]\n\nLet me search specifically for OR-Tools GitHub repository build configuration.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - pypa/manylinux: Python wheels that work on any linux (almost) · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/pypa/manylinux\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/cmake at main · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/tree/main/cmake\"},{\"title\":\"[CMake] CMake and manylinux Python Wheels\",\"url\":\"https://cmake.org/pipermail/cmake/2018-August/068168.html\"},{\"title\":\"Building python wheels for many linux-es\",\"url\":\"https://gmagno.github.io/2019/01/building-python-wheels-for-many-linux-es/\"},{\"title\":\"[CMake] CMake and manylinux Python Wheels\",\"url\":\"https://cmake.cmake.narkive.com/yDb1dVV6/and-manylinux-python-wheels\"},{\"title\":\"Add official Python 3.14 wheels (Linux/macOS/Windows) for OR-Tools · Issue #4859 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4859\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Klebert-Engineering/python-cmake-wheel: CMake helper for cross-platform binary Python packages 🐍.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Klebert-Engineering/python-cmake-wheel\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - scikit-build/cmake-python-distributions: This project provides the infrastructure to build CMake Python wheels. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/scikit-build/cmake-python-distributions\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/cmake/README.md at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/cmake/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Assistance building pygmo2 wheels with cibuildwheel - Packaging - Discussions on Python.org\",\"url\":\"https://discuss.python.org/t/assistance-building-pygmo2-wheels-with-cibuildwheel/21714\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I've gathered information about manylinux wheel building and general PGO/LTO optimization practices, but I haven't found specific documentation about OR-Tools 9.x 2025 releases with particular build flags. Let me provide a comprehensive summary of what was found:\n\n## Summary of Search Results\n\nI performed a web search for information about OR-Tools manylinux wheel building with PGO and LTO optimization flags. Here's what I found:\n\n### OR-Tools Releases\n\nOR-Tools v9.15 was released, and OR-Tools version 9.15.6755 was released on January 14, 2026. Version 9.12 (2025/02) was the last release to support Python 3.8, and Python 3.13 support was added, and musllinux wheel packages were introduced.\n\n### Manylinux Wheel Building\n\nNative python modules on Linux must only dynamically link a set of libraries and symbols called manylinux and musllinux to ensure wheels are portable. OR-Tools comes with a CMake-based build (CMakeLists.txt) that can be used on a wide range of platforms.\n\n### PGO and LTO Optimization\n\nWhile the search results don't contain specific documentation about OR-Tools using PGO or LTO flags, they do show general best practices:\n\nMaturin supports building with Profile-Guided Optimization (PGO), which performs a three-phase build: instrumented build, profile training, and optimized rebuild. CMake options for PGO builds can include flags like \"-flto -fprofile-use=<path>\".\n\nThe search results do not contain specific information about whether OR-Tools 9.x currently uses PGO or LTO flags in its manylinux wheel builds. You may need to check the OR-Tools GitHub repository directly for current build configuration details.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b5cd1ee1-c27b-451f-adfc-843b8b4b4fc5","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:03:50.493Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0455b956-65c2-4174-b15e-93a7c2cfdfa4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
